# Guide for Coding Agents

## CDD policy

This project follows Contract-Driven Development (CDD).

- Detailed protocol: `.agents/workflow/cdd.md`
- Concept reference: `.claude/skills/sonamu/cdd.md`
- Start CDD work: `/cdd` slash command

## Canonical control files

- Primary instructions: `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/`
- `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/` are compatibility symlinks — do not edit them directly

## Core workflow

1. Delegate planning to `cdd-planner`
2. Orchestrator converts approved plan into Claims (`tmp/claims/`)
3. surface → (surface review) → test + implement (parallel) → stage reviews → integration review → AC verification

## TypeScript type safety policy

- `as any` and `as unknown as T` are strictly prohibited
- Non-null assertion (`!`) is prohibited — use optional chaining (`?.`) or type guards

## Commit message policy

- Format: `[scope] type: short title`
- Messages in Korean
- No Co-Authored-By trailers

## Absolute prohibitions

- Do not edit generated files (`*.generated.ts`, `sonamu.generated.*`)
- Do not execute migrations without explicit user confirmation
- Do not deploy
